body:
Hi. I found a weird problem. 
This is my listener: 

```js
document.addEventListener('click', (e) => {
  
  if (e.target.matches('.click-analytics')) {
    let correct_position = 1 + parseInt(e.target.getAttribute('data-position'));
    window.aa('click', {
      objectID: e.target.getAttribute('data-objectid'),
      position: correct_position,
    })
    console.log(e.target.getAttribute('data-objectid'));
  } 
  else if (e.target.matches('.conversion-analytics')) {
    window.aa('conversion', {
      objectID: e.target.getAttribute('data-objectid'),
    })
    console.log(e.target.getAttribute('data-objectid'));
  }
})
```

that is part of my hit template: 
 ```html
<div class="hit-content">
              <div class="hit-image">
                <a class="click-analytics" data-objectid="{{objectID}}" data-position="{{__hitIndex}}" href="{{url}}"><img src="{{image}}" alt="{{name}}"></a>
              </div>
              <a class="click-analytics" data-objectid="{{objectID}}" data-position="{{__hitIndex}}" href="{{url}}">lalals</a>
                <h2 class="hit-name"><a class="click-analytics" data-objectid="{{objectID}}" data-position="{{__hitIndex}}" href="{{url}}">{{name}}</a></h2> 
```
And the problem is:
When i click on .hit-name or div with "lalals" text. It seems work well. I got console message: `91722`
But when i click on image (.hit-image) it doesn't work. (i don't get console.log message).
